Day 19 Notes – Local Storage in React

1.Import useEffect
import { useState, useEffect } from "react";

2.Load data from Local Storage (on start)
const [todos, setTodos] = useState(() => {
const saved = localStorage.getItem("todos");
return saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : [];
});

3.Save data whenever todos change
useEffect(() => {
localStorage.setItem("todos", JSON.stringify(todos));
}, [todos]);

4.Important Methods:
localStorage.setItem("key", value)
localStorage.getItem("key")
JSON.stringify() → convert to string
JSON.parse() → convert back to array/object

5.useEffect Dependency
useEffect(() => {
// code
}, [todos]);


-Runs every time todos changes
Key Point:
useEffect + localStorage = data stays even after page refresh.
